/*

# pyproject.toml is NOT re-included here on purpose. Git already tracks it,
# and .gitignore does not touch tracked files. A '!/pyproject.toml' line would
# instead undo the exclusion that flwr applies to the same file when it builds
# the FAB: the file would end up in the bundle twice and break its hash check
# ("Duplicate name: 'pyproject.toml'", "File hashes couldn't be verified").
# In a fresh clone made from scratch, add it once with: git add -f pyproject.toml

!/.gitignore
!/README.md

!/*.py
!/*.ps1
!/requirements-lock.txt
!/uv.lock

!/figures/
!/notebooks/
!/qibo_qfl_pt/
!/run_experiments/
!/thesis_plots/


__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/


*.json
*.npz
*.png
*.pdf
*.csv
*.tex
*.log

!/figures/*.png